        "id": 1,
        "title": "Architectural Domain Separation & Transport Distinction",
        "type": "row"
      },
      {
        "description": "Architectural guidelines defining the separation between network transport and voice application health. A successful TCP/TLS handshake to SBC port 5061 proves only layer-4 socket reachability. It does not verify SIP registration, digest authentication, codec negotiation, or bidirectional media flow. Missing data indicates collector outage, agent failure, or network disruption; values are preserved as null gaps.",
        "gridPos": {
          "h": 4,
          "w": 24,
          "x": 0,
          "y": 1
        },
        "id": 2,
        "options": {
          "content": "> \u26a0\ufe0f **Domain Boundary Notice: Layer 4/7 Transport vs Media & Telephony Health**\n>\n> A successful TCP 3-way handshake or TLS session negotiation to Avaya SBCE port 5061 (`endpoint.service.reachable = 1`) proves **only** that socket connectivity exists across the network perimeter.\n>\n> It does **NOT** verify:\n> 1. SIP User Agent Digest Authentication or SIP Registration state.\n> 2. SDP offer/answer codec negotiation (e.g. G.711 A-law / G.729).\n> 3. NAT traversal or asymmetric media routing (e.g. one-way RTP audio).\n> 4. End-to-end voice quality (ITU-T G.107 MOS) or packet jitter.\n>\n> Comprehensive voice service assurance correlates **both** endpoint edge reachability and controlled synthetic Asterisk call probes.",
          "mode": "markdown"
        },
        "pluginVersion": "11.6.0",
        "title": "Voice Observability Domain Boundary",
        "type": "text"
      },
      {
        "collapsed": false,
        "gridPos": {
          "h": 1,
          "w": 24,
          "x": 0,
          "y": 5
        },
        "id": 3,
        "title": "Real-Time Service Assurance & Status Overview",
        "type": "row"
      },
      {
        "datasource": {
          "type": "alexanderzobnin-zabbix-datasource",
          "uid": "PA67C5EADE9207728"
        },
        "description": "Reports the signaling and media result of controlled Asterisk synthetic voice probes (ANSWERED, BUSY, CONGESTION, TIMEOUT, FAILED). A healthy result confirms end-to-end SIP signaling and call setup across the voice core. CONGESTION (SIP 503) or TIMEOUT (SIP 408) indicates trunk capacity exhaustion or core server unreachability. Missing data indicates collector outage, agent failure, or network disruption; values are preserved as null gaps.",
        "fieldConfig": {
          "defaults": {
            "color": {
              "mode": "thresholds"
            },
            "mappings": [
              {
                "options": {
                  "ANSWERED": {
                    "color": "green",
                    "text": "ANSWERED (HEALTHY)"
                  },
                  "BUSY": {
                    "color": "yellow",
                    "text": "BUSY (USER REJECT)"
                  },
                  "CONGESTION": {
                    "color": "red",
                    "text": "CONGESTION (SIP 503)"
                  },
                  "FAILED": {
                    "color": "red",
                    "text": "FAILED"
                  },
                  "TIMEOUT": {
                    "color": "red",
                    "text": "TIMEOUT (SIP 408)"
                  }
                },
                "type": "value"
              }
            ],
            "noValue": "STALE / NO DATA",
            "thresholds": {
