        "description": "Calculates Mean Opinion Score (1.0 to 4.5) using ITU-T G.107 E-model based on measured RTP packet loss, jitter, and delay. Scores below 3.8 indicate noticeable degradation; scores below 3.5 indicate unacceptable voice quality. Crucially, displays UNKNOWN when RTCP reports are missing to avoid fabricating voice quality metrics. Missing data indicates collector outage, agent failure, or network disruption; values are preserved as null gaps.",
